  #line-at(351pt, 204.06pt, "Fig. 2e")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.97pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(382.68pt, 204.06pt, "), which is sufficiently fast for gate ")
  #line-at(72pt, 216.72pt, "driving of power transistors. The full-bridge rectifier converts the received RF output back into an electrical ")
  #line-at(72pt, 229.38pt, "PWM signal for given load (i.e. the gate of a GaN HEMT) which enables simultaneous electric power and ")
  #line-at(72pt, 242.04pt, "encoded control signal transmission. We characterize output performance of our device by measuring its ")
  #line-at(72pt, 254.7pt, "current-voltage (I-V) response under various load conditions (")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.97pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(352.86pt, 254.7pt, "Fig. 2f")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.97pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(383.82pt, 254.7pt, "). Our SAW device behaves like a ")
  #line-at(72pt, 267.36pt, "voltage source with a slightly nonlinear internal resistance, providing an open-circuit voltage of 13.4 V and ")
  #line-at(72pt, 279.96pt, "a short circuit current of 44.4 mA at the receiver end, which eliminates the need for separate bulky isolated ")
  #line-at(72pt, 292.62pt, "power supplies. ")
  #line-at(72pt, 313.26pt, "      We characterize the isolation performance of our devices. The breakdown voltages of our SAW devices ")
