  #line-at(72pt, 186.78pt, "Methods ")
  #line-at(72pt, 205.44pt, "SAW Device fabrication and characterization ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.01pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 217.2pt, "Our device is fabricated on 128°Y cut black LN substrate, and the SAW is propagating in the crystal X direction. The ")
  #line-at(72pt, 228.66pt, "IDT aperture is 500 μm, with 20 pairs of finger electrodes distributed in a pitch of 8.55 μm, corresponding to an ")
  #line-at(72pt, 240.18pt, "acoustic frequency of 223 MHz. The device is patterned using a maskless aligner (Heidelberg Instruments MLA 150) ")
  #line-at(72pt, 251.7pt, "using photoresist (Microposit S1818), followed by electron beam evaporation of 10-nm-thick chrome and 90-nm-")
  #line-at(72pt, 263.16pt, "thick gold, and lift-off process using Microposit Remover 1165. ")
  #line-at(72pt, 274.68pt, "      The 223-MHz input RF signals are generated by a vector signal generator (Rohde & Schwarz SMW200A). The ")
  #line-at(72pt, 286.2pt, "RF signals are then modulated by square waves from an arbitrary waveform generator (Rigol DG 852 Pro). The ")
  #line-at(72pt, 297.66pt, "modulated signals are amplified by 53 dB using a high power RF amplifier (Mini-circuits ZHL-10M2G0020+) before ")
  #line-at(72pt, 309.18pt, "delivering to the input port of our SAW device.")
  #line-at(72pt, 320.7pt, "      The microwave performance of the SAW devices at room temperature is characterized using a home-built probe ")
  #line-at(72pt, 332.16pt, "station with microwave instruments. We use a network analyzer (Keysight 5000A or LibreVNA 2.0) to measure the ")
